## Appendix 3: System Testing Evidence

Detailed System Testing test cases and supporting evidence are provided in this appendix, which are not covered in Section 4.3.1. The System Testing has been performed according to seven categories: E2E Workflow, Integration, Performance, Recovery, Business Logic, Reporting and Compliance. All 34 System Testing test cases achieved a Pass result. For brevity, one test case from each of the testing groups is given in Section 4.3.1, with the remaining test cases and evidence presented in Appendix 3.1 to Appendix 3.7, grouped by testing category.

### Appendix 3.1 E2E Workflow

The remaining End-to-End (E2E) Workflow System Testing test cases are provided in this appendix which are not covered by Section 4.3.1.1. These test cases are used to provide supporting evidence for the end-to-end EasyEarn user workflows for Job Seeker, Employer and Admin functions. Additional test cases are provided below, with the representative E2E Workflow test case, ST-003: Hire-to-completion flow, presented in Section 4.3.1.1.

ST-001: Job seeker registration to application

This test covers the complete Job Seeker workflow from account registration and profile completion to browsing job listings and submitting an application. Ensures that the application is properly documented and in the Applications section with a pending status. The job seeker's profile form and completed profile are depicted in Figure A3.1 along with the completed application submitted with a "pending" status.

![Figure 1](Appendix Diagram/figure-01.png)

Figure A3.1: Registration of the job seeker as an applicant

ST-002: Employer registration to applicant review

Handles onboarding of the employer with a secure employer code, posting job listings, and the employer reviews incoming applicants. Ensures proper gating of registration and that applicant status updates are communicated to the seeker. The employer registration with the secure employer code, posted job listing, and the applicant review screen are illustrated in Figure A3.2.

![Figure 2](Appendix Diagram/figure-02.png)

Figure A3.2: Registration of the job seeker as an applicant

ST-004: Admin moderation lifecycle

Consists of an admin who reviews a reported job listing, suspends it and resolves the report. Confirms that the listing is no longer visible when publicly searching for a listing and the report is marked resolved with notes saved. The admin moderation screen for a reported listing with the suspend action and resolved report, along with saved notes, is depicted in Figure A3.3.

![Figure 3](Appendix Diagram/figure-03.png)

Figure A3.3: Admin Moderation Lifecycle

ST-005: Payment lifecycle

Completes the two-step payment confirmation: employer marks payment as paid, seeker confirms receipt. Ensures both times are independently recorded, and payment is not "confirmed" until the seeker acts. The two-step payment confirmation is shown in Figure A3.4: the employer's "Mark as Paid" action and the independent receipt confirmation.

![Figure 4](Appendix Diagram/figure-04.png)

Figure A3.4: Payment Lifecycle

ST-006: Payment dispute and resolution

Covers a seeker who raises a payment dispute rather than confirming receipt, and admin mediation. Validates that the report is correct for the correct application/payment, without changing the payment state. The payment dispute submission and correct payment/record view for admin mediation are shown in Figure A3.5.

![Figure 5](Appendix Diagram/figure-05.png)

Figure A3.5: Payment Dispute and Resolution

